1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,013
Open the Shared device settings at sign-in and enter a recognizable device label.

2
00:00:05,193 --> 00:00:09,588
This fictional dispatch workstation is the Academy Dispatch handoff desk.

3
00:00:09,768 --> 00:00:10,877
Choose Save.

4
00:00:11,197 --> 00:00:13,629
Check the saved label on the sign-in form.

5
00:00:13,809 --> 00:00:19,164
Each dispatcher uses their own account so the application can track the active operator.

6
00:00:19,484 --> 00:00:22,385
During the shift, open Settings and find Session.

7
00:00:22,565 --> 00:00:25,296
Choose Lock when you step away from the workstation.

8
00:00:25,476 --> 00:00:30,489
The same step can help at a shared security desk or community coordination center.

9
00:00:30,809 --> 00:00:33,796
The locked screen shows which operator is signed in.

10
00:00:33,976 --> 00:00:37,261
This example has no eligible verification method.

11
00:00:37,441 --> 00:00:43,500
Choose End shift to return to sign-in, or use Switch operator when another operator is taking over.

12
00:00:43,820 --> 00:00:48,151
Verify that the sign-in form returns and the desk label is still visible.

13
00:00:48,331 --> 00:00:51,445
The next operator can now sign in for their own shift.
